{"t": 1794109144.8228598, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_add_issue_comment", "args": {"body": "Fixed the red `contract-tests` check on this PR.\n\n**What failed:** `contract/test_fee_contract.py::test_fee_rounding_contract` \u2014 `fee(2.675)` returned `2.67`, but the card-network contract (PAY-88) requires fees to be computed on exact decimal values and rounded HALF-UP to cents, i.e. `2.68`. The float-based code was rounding the binary approximation of `2.675` (`2.67499999...`), so `round()` went down instead of up.\n\n**What I changed** (`payments/fees.py`, committed to `fees-float`):\n- Replaced binary-float rounding with `Decimal`: `Decimal(str(amount))` keeps the decimal value exact, then `.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_UP)` applies the contract's rounding mode.\n- Behaviour now: `fee(2.675) == 2.68`, `fee(1.005) == 1.01`, `fee(100.0) == 100.0` (unchanged).\n- `python -m pytest -q` passes locally.\n\nNo test changes and no public API change \u2014 `fee()` still takes and returns a float.", "issue_number": 214, "owner": "acme", "repo": "payments"}, "ok": true}
